<title>FRANCE: Suez sells Salins shares at 614 Ffr/shr.</title>
<headline>Suez sells Salins shares at 614 Ffr/shr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>French company Cie de Suez said it had sold on Thursday morning 1.259 million shares in Salins du Midi for 614 francs per share, for a total of 773 million francs.</p>
<p>The sale followed an agreement signed on December 31, 1996, it said in a statement. The shares, which represented all of Suez's holding in Salins, had been held by Suez wholly-owned unit Suez Industrie.</p>
<p>U.S. company Morton International acquired control of the French saltmaker late last year.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
</text>
